{"lines":[{"h":0.022144506339892067,"x":0.84005194080655299,"y":0.061502263684855674,"t":"Reading","w":0.083682918548584007,"c":1},{"w":0.75533645629882806,"c":1,"y":0.10889648733676338,"h":0.022461658653016747,"t":"UK companies need more effective boards of directors","x":0.12542593858856738},{"x":0.10891579516520229,"w":0.77802266438802081,"t":"After a number of serious failures of governance (that is, how they are managed","c":1,"h":0.022180370784620207,"y":0.14639834554004583},{"w":0.75950444539388029,"x":0.13155000368577655,"t":"at the highest level), companies in Britain, as well as elsewhere, should consider","y":0.16610531739721801,"h":0.020810703506739303,"c":1},{"t":"radical changes to their directors' roles. It is clear that the role of a board director","h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.12962962242969156,"y":0.18459302300407465,"w":0.7613168843587238,"c":1},{"h":0.021443031140294888,"c":1,"w":0.77801579793294273,"t":"today is not an easy one. Following the 2008 financial meltdown, which resulted in","x":0.12745759629094494,"y":0.20022257142843558},{"y":0.21851483923268844,"x":0.12950863726544573,"t":"a deeper and more prolonged period of economic downturn than anyone expected,","w":0.78628819783528636,"h":0.021372081815002941,"c":1},{"t":"the search for explanations in the many post-mortems of the crisis has meant","w":0.73456792195638021,"x":0.12757200597744012,"y":0.23837209287689642,"h":0.016044868316470673,"c":1},{"w":0.77388600667317708,"h":0.021639530734544166,"t":"blame has been spread far and wide. Governments, regulators, central banks and","x":0.12950113749707989,"c":1,"y":0.25427506909847408},{"t":"auditors have all been in the frame. The role of bank directors and management","h":0.02061589895906657,"x":0.12952208298495918,"w":0.75536834716796875,"y":0.27182752672488486,"c":1},{"x":0.12747838671127038,"y":0.28994811854966596,"h":0.02027206286103489,"w":0.69977661132812496,"c":1,"t":"and their widely publicised failures have been extensively picked over and"},{"h":0.021386001640832042,"x":0.12744404831278633,"c":1,"w":0.47139872233072921,"y":0.30669762975684722,"t":"examined in reports, inquiries and commentaries."},{"t":"The knock-on effect of this scrutiny has been to make the governance of","y":0.33486676414134453,"x":0.12741216517293735,"h":0.020536568757361651,"c":1,"w":0.68549026489257803},{"x":0.12746521889649423,"y":0.35271334518589992,"w":0.72039515177408864,"h":0.020722572317673826,"t":"companies in general an issue of intense public debate and has significantly","c":1},{"y":0.37070481082405893,"c":1,"t":"increased the pressures on, and the responsibilities of, directors. At the simplest","x":0.12536392563820101,"w":0.75954940795898451,"h":0.021410840981419543},{"x":0.12551439360103955,"w":0.72839508056640634,"t":"and most practical level, the time involved in fulfilling the demands of a board","h":0.017441860778592999,"c":1,"y":0.38953488355715893},{"w":0.75737096150716143,"x":0.12542349799737604,"t":"directorship has increased significantly, calling into question the effectiveness of","y":0.4066929082152142,"h":0.021717028848133646,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.022514675755944458,"t":"the classic model of corporate governance by part-time, independent non-executive","y":0.42370612050270418,"w":0.79025558471679691,"x":0.12545036836885742},{"x":0.12539620417007938,"t":"directors. Where once a board schedule may have consisted of between eight and","c":1,"y":0.44197539793700313,"h":0.020568324202502763,"w":0.78005411783854173},{"t":"ten meetings a year, in many companies the number of events requiring board","x":0.1233814688222958,"c":1,"y":0.46051360921130668,"w":0.74293329874674474,"h":0.01946046467523832},{"h":0.020843723777887901,"t":"input and decisions has dramatically risen. Furthermore, the amount of reading","x":0.12331913096326863,"c":1,"y":0.47739925208186251,"w":0.74721537272135419},{"c":1,"t":"and preparation required for each meeting is increasing. Agendas can become","w":0.74296259562174471,"x":0.12543403257509284,"y":0.49581811391116948,"h":0.019430695209121218},{"y":0.51240033795835627,"x":0.1253718554453053,"t":"overloaded and this can mean the time for constructive debate must necessarily be","w":0.78629857381184898,"h":0.021301249312006498,"c":1},{"x":0.12345679188894512,"h":0.016039732066986834,"w":0.48765431722005204,"t":"restricted in favour of getting through the business.","y":0.53343023241002152,"c":1},{"w":0.69566660563151039,"t":"Often, board business is devolved to committees in order to cope with the","h":0.01963203169572203,"c":1,"x":0.12541115134553601,"y":0.55950598051935041},{"c":1,"h":0.01750691675606264,"y":0.57848837192987246,"t":"workload, which may be more efficient but can mean that the board as a whole","x":0.12345679490182837,"w":0.74485595703124996},{"y":0.59363834601805798,"h":0.02070264063679006,"w":0.73894220987955728,"t":"is less involved in fully addressing some of the most important issues. It is not","c":1,"x":0.12127563505996761},{"c":1,"x":0.1234567878344825,"y":0.61482558124883724,"w":0.7366255187988282,"t":"uncommon for the audit committee meeting to last longer than the main board","h":0.01598837238037687},{"x":0.12345678960183203,"y":0.63074204974910908,"h":0.017513764339846971,"t":"meeting itself. Process may take the place of discussion and be at the expense of","w":0.77572016398111987,"c":1},{"t":"real collaboration, so that boxes are ticked rather than issues tackled.","w":0.66255142211914064,"c":1,"y":0.6495877502391102,"h":0.019140164899882239,"x":0.12139918595959803},{"t":"A radical solution, which may work for some very large companies whose","x":0.11111111341646109,"y":0.67726737340128507,"w":0.70576131184895829,"c":1,"h":0.017500068610632802},{"x":0.12139918435865146,"y":0.69611307445017967,"t":"businesses are extensive and complex, is the professional board, whose members","h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"w":0.78395060221354163},{"y":0.71366279054960524,"x":0.12139918429378545,"w":0.78395060221354174,"h":0.016019188192342826,"c":1,"t":"would work up to three or four days a week, supported by their own dedicated staff"},{"h":0.015988372380376759,"x":0.12139916799630177,"t":"and advisers. There are obvious risks to this and it would be important to establish","y":0.73110465101542998,"c":1,"w":0.77983540852864575},{"t":"clear guidelines for such a board to ensure that it did not step on the toes of","y":0.74811429327670087,"w":0.7182444254557292,"x":0.1213305669877271,"c":1,"h":0.018263070968070783},{"w":0.77589757283528649,"h":0.019569430671395383,"t":"management by becoming too engaged in the day-to-day running of the company.","y":0.76546272923154901,"x":0.12132472189613641,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.018190971392484379,"x":0.12134001173639282,"w":0.78406585693359365,"t":"Problems of recruitment, remuneration and independence could also arise and this","y":0.78339885787027419},{"t":"structure would not be appropriate for all companies. However, more professional","y":0.8005353336818084,"x":0.12126137594079581,"w":0.77186192830403644,"h":0.021551684861469633,"c":1},{"x":0.12123199155629814,"w":0.74522755940755203,"t":"and better-informed boards would have been particularly appropriate for banks","y":0.81569191142604214,"c":1,"h":0.023304396720320142},{"t":"where the executives had access to information that part-time non-executive","x":0.11934156333982211,"c":1,"h":0.016017476296396826,"y":0.83863368663493798,"w":0.72427983601888013},{"t":"directors lacked, leaving the latter unable to comprehend or","h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"x":0.11934155327272748,"w":0.56790125528971358,"y":0.85600706731595655},{"y":0.87295258735931658,"x":0.11905300944149687,"t":"crash.","w":0.064363117218017588,"h":0.017176220358049887,"c":1},{"t":"leltsresources.org","x":0.39483721299237268,"y":0.96768258536995222,"h":0.016454192297478354,"c":1,"w":0.20824633280436194}],"w":2400,"h":3395}